Don’t call people more than twice.
If they didn’t pick up, they saw it.

2. Stop being overly nice
to everyone.
Kindness without limits turns into weakness.

3. Don’t share what you know unless someone asks.
Most people just want attention, not advice.

4. Never explain yourself. If you need to - you already lost power.

5. Keep your plans to yourself. Talk after it’s done.

6. Don’t try to be “needed.” Be someone people choose.

7. Stop trying to please everyone.
Respect is born from boundaries, not approval.

8. Do only what feels right... not what looks right.

9. If someone adds real value to your life, thank them even for the small stuff.

10. Always keep your word. That’s how trust is built. Live with boundaries. Act from respect, not from need. Talk less, move sharper.
